(ENTERPRISE CYBERSECURITY & ACCESS GOVERNANCE POLICY) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 710 Td
(1. PURPOSE & SCOPE) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 690 Td
(This policy defines mandatory security requirements for corporate network access, data handling,) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 675 Td
(and remote device management across all internal departments and third-party contractors.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 650 Td
(2. MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS & AUTHENTICATION) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 630 Td
(- Multi-Factor Authentication \(MFA\) is strictly mandatory for all employees and system administrators.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 615 Td
(- Acceptable MFA methods include hardware security keys \(FIDO2\) and authenticator apps \(TOTP\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 600 Td
(- SMS-based OTP verification is prohibited for administrative roles due to SIM-swapping vulnerabilities.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 585 Td
(- Passwords must be at least 16 characters in length and updated every 90 days.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 560 Td
(3. SECURE REMOTE ACCESS & ENCRYPTION) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 540 Td
(- All remote connections must traverse the corporate encrypted VPN tunnel with TLS 1.3 enabled.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 525 Td
(- Unmanaged personal devices \(BYOD\) are strictly forbidden from directly connecting to production servers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 510 Td
(- Confidential data stored on laptops or portable drives must use AES-256 full-disk encryption.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 485 Td
(4. INCIDENT REPORTING & COMPLIANCE ACTIONS) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 465 Td
(- Any suspected credential compromise or phishing attempt must be reported to SOC within 15 minutes.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 450 Td
(- Employees must complete mandatory bi-annual security awareness and phishing simulations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9 Tf
60 435 Td
(- Failure to adhere to this policy will result in immediate revocation of access privileges.) Tj
ET

